{"summary":"Accept the documentation/provenance clarifications and reject the two amendments whose defect claims are contradicted by the current validation and shrimp-stress code paths.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8014730a","decision":"accept","rationale":"`coarse_porous.toml` allows `colonizable_area_factor` up to 1.1, but the notes only describe footprint-scaled habitat value and the shipped preset sits at 0.9. Because values above 1.0 are semantically surprising unless porous-media surface area is explicitly intended, either documenting that meaning or tightening the cap improves correctness and maintainability."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d7c5dd73","decision":"accept","rationale":"Adding an explicit 25°C reference value next to the temperature-dependent `pKa1(T)` formula is a safe documentation improvement. It makes the provenance table easier to cross-check against standard carbonate references and matches the presentation style already used for `PKA2`."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1c025102","decision":"reject","rationale":"The cited validation defect is not present. `temp_condition_low_divisor_c` and `temp_condition_high_divisor_c` are validated in the positive-only bucket, while the `<= 1.0` bucket covers different fields. The shipped shrimp preset values `10.0` and `8.0` therefore do not get rejected by the current validator."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-f229f75f","decision":"reject","rationale":"The new NH3 tuning already reaches molt-related behavior through the condition path. Hourly NH3 stress feeds `update_condition`, the daily pipeline runs `update_condition` before `update_molt_stress`, and both `update_molt_stress` and `molt_cycle` consume condition. So changing the NH3 threshold/scale can affect `molt_stress_index`, warning emission, and molt success even though `hourly_pressure` itself only includes heat and instability."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7893222b","decision":"accept","rationale":"These newly exposed shrimp tuning parameters have no corresponding `[param_meta.*]` entries in `neocaridina_davidi.toml`. Adding provenance metadata or explicit provisional notes improves auditability and is consistent with the repository’s stated expectation that new preset parameters carry per-parameter metadata."}]}